Test whether the sound plays to headphones

WebRTC patch 0018 (the audio device modules) has the Core Audio module tell
PlayoutToHeadphones from the playout endpoint's form factor.
test/playout_form_factor.test.cc (Windows only) drives
AudioDeviceWindowsCore::DeviceStateListener with a fake endpoint and property store, so no
audio device is needed: headphones and a headset play to headphones; speakers, line level,
a handset, S/PDIF, a display, an unknown or unlisted form factor do not, nor does a store
that gives no value (VT_EMPTY), another type (VT_I4), a failure or no store at all. The
answer follows the endpoint when it says another form factor (its id compared without
case) and when its state changes (unplugged, disabled or not present give no; active again
reads it anew); another key or another endpoint reads nothing, and nothing is read once
playout stops, which sets no. The listener holds the endpoint only while playing and lets
the store go after each read. A state change also counts as a change of devices (patch
0011); the tests that read that count take it from their start.

